From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:51:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: optional diagnostic heap and build label for test
 builds

The diag-alloc feature (off by default) routes every Rust allocation
through exec AllocVec so mungwall walls each block, adds tail canaries,
a checked quarantine for freed blocks and two self-tests, and frees the
remaining blocks after the pthread exit handler, where the C library's
pool goes away in the normal build. Findings raise a recoverable alert
and are appended to RAM:PdfCraft-diag.txt.

PDFCRAFT_AROS_LABEL adds a label to the version shown by --version, the
window title and $VER, so a screenshot names the build variant.
